<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#4F545C\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">AngryIcecream</span></span></span></div><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#B9BBBE\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">#7377</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T14:32:31-08:00","id":1169476,"title":"","content":"I set my bio and I invite people to add to it by joining. Our characters could have met the day he lost his sister.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T06:27:13-08:00","id":1169613,"title":"","content":"I am interested in joining. Is this game still taking submissions?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> In the Far East, in the territory near the shadowland known as the Noss Fens, there are a number of villages where the native tongue is not Forest-Tounge but rather Old Realm. This is not because they have somehow kept that ancient tongue intact, rather it is because the Dowager of the Irreverent Vulgate in Unrent Veils teaches Old Realm to them every generation and harshly punishes any deviation from what she deems correct. Hope's Last Gasp is from one of those villages, and she is thusly one of the Dowager's \u201cchildren\u201d.<br /> <br /> Her early life was pleasant enough, she had both parents as well as an older brother and an identical twin sister. She learned her chores and enjoyed herself as most children do.<br /> <br /> Then the Dowager came. The entire village was captured, and the Dowager made the children watch as their parents and older loved ones were turned into soulsteel trinkets. Then they were forced to give up their names to the neverborn. Thus did Rose become Hope's Last Gasp.<br /> <br /> Yet where there is life, there is hope, and Hope's Last Gasp can last for a very long time indeed. She learned and refined the art of not being heard, and not being seen. She memorized the location of her family's souls and the patrol routes of the guards. And then finally, she felt herself ready, and she snuck herself, her sister, and the cutlery that was her family's remains out of the Dowager's citadel.<br /> <br /> She would have gotten away cleanly too, if she hadn't exalted at the tail end of her escape. In the ensuing chaos, she got away, but her sister died to the arrows of the guards. She found herself guided by past life memories and intuition to a safe house demense with a cache of useful items, and cried herself to sleep.<br /> <br /> When she woke in the morning, she was filled with resolve to retrieve her sister's remains. But instead found her sister had become the Shoat of the Mire. Anguished, she ran away, first just to get away, but eventually she changed her purpose to finding someone who could help her get her sister away from the Dowager. Her first companion was a cat that basically adopted her.<br /> <br /> Her wanderings have taken her south, towards the dreaming sea.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T12:16:48-08:00","id":1169699,"title":"","content":"I'll be joining you guys too, still need to figure out the details about my char over christmas though. It'll likely be a sneaky night caste","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T12:40:57-08:00","id":1169706,"title":"","content":"@Aranfan: Your character back-story looks good. My only question is; Shoat of the Mire, is that her sister as one of the Dowager's deathknights?<br /> <br /> @Flinty: it's all good. Post your character here when they're complete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T15:06:30-08:00","id":1169740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1168272-ooc-exalted-3e-the-pirates-of-the-gilded-throne?p=1169706#post1169706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Aranfan: Your character back-story looks good. My only question is; Shoat of the Mire, is that her sister as one of the Dowager's deathknights?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The purpose of a backstory is to give the GM plothooks to push the story along with. <br /> <br /> Also, I would like to request a custom charm that's basically Vile Anathema Shroud from 2e but indefinite. If that's okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T15:18:09-08:00","id":1169745,"title":"","content":"I added to my bio how Laughter and Hope met Scholar. It was on an attack by the Fae that the three met.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T14:51:04-08:00","id":1170025,"title":"","content":"Once I get an answer on the custom charm I'll upload a sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T20:26:53-08:00","id":1170074,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11917_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11917\" data-vbnamecard=\"11917\">Aranfan</a> : That's fine, The custom charm will have Phantom Hood Technique as a prereq. <br /> <br /> Everything is looking good so far. Does anyone have any other questions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T21:23:18-08:00","id":1170083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1168272-ooc-exalted-3e-the-pirates-of-the-gilded-throne?p=1170074#post1170074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11917_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11917\" data-vbnamecard=\"11917\">Aranfan</a> : That's fine, The custom charm will have Phantom Hood Technique as a prereq.<br /> <br /> Everything is looking good so far. Does anyone have any other questions?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Drat, she's stealth supernal so that won't work.<br /> <br /> I just want her to pass as an abyssal. Ah well. I'll put together a sheet now and post it in the morning after I've woken up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T04:54:25-08:00","id":1170144,"title":"","content":"We really do not lack night castes, it seems.<br /> <br /> Edit: To give you guys a rough idea, I'm probably going to play the reincarnation of Shadows Grace. My char will be a reluctant assassin in the employ of Five Days Darkness (also supernaling Stealth and using Ebon Shadow style)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11917_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11917\" data-vbnamecard=\"11917\">Aranfan</a><br /> You could take an artifact that helps you masquerade as an abyssal. If that's its only function then its probably around 3dot rating.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 12-24-2017, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T07:11:01-08:00","id":1170164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1168272-ooc-exalted-3e-the-pirates-of-the-gilded-throne?p=1170144#post1170144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We really do not lack night castes, it seems.<br /> <br /> Edit: To give you guys a rough idea, I'm probably going to play the reincarnation of Shadows Grace. My char will be a reluctant assassin in the employ of Five Days Darkness (also supernaling Stealth and using Ebon Shadow style)<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span><br /> You could take an artifact that helps you masquerade as an abyssal. If that's its only function then its probably around 3dot rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. It seems on the question of Pirates vs Ninjas, the answer is that Ninjas ARE Pirates, after all.<br /> <br /> As per your desire to look like an Abyssal, there, Aranfan, I apologize if I disrupted your plans, but looking at Vile Anathema Shroud and it's ability placement, and seeing the Solar larceny tree, that's what made the most sense to me. <br /> <br /> As per Flinty's idea, that's an option, as would having evocations, especially for a soulsteel artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T08:09:07-08:00","id":1170178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1168272-ooc-exalted-3e-the-pirates-of-the-gilded-throne?p=1170164#post1170164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. It seems on the question of Pirates vs Ninjas, the answer is that Ninjas ARE Pirates, after all.<br /> <br /> As per Flinty's idea, that's an option, as would having evocations, especially for a soulsteel artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's that comic where a pirate crew has a ninja that assasinates captians before boarding?<br /> <br /> As to the evocation, The cutlery set that is most of her family is soulsteel. I had planned on it being a two dot that just sterilizes the food it's used to eat with, but I can make it a 3 dot. I kinda just want Mom to be a mundane knife that's made out of soulsteel. But if it's three dot I might as well make her a light artifact weapon. Hmm.<br /> <br /> Edit: Maybe artifact stats for Mom can be a later evocation?<br /> <br /> edit2: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1j3O0hqxmYFkU2nT8tGS0LyhXEv5YrGOp/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1j3O...ew?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 12-24-2017, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T09:00:05-08:00","id":1170192,"title":"","content":"That would be an excellent idea. Heck, I'd allow the set itself to be a collective weapon if you'd like. That it also contains the souls of your family would make sense as to masking you as an Abyssal, as they're trying to mask your power if invonvenient. I'll leave it up to you if you want to make your cutlery a weapon or not, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T09:06:11-08:00","id":1170193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1168272-ooc-exalted-3e-the-pirates-of-the-gilded-throne?p=1170192#post1170192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be an excellent idea. Heck, I'd allow the set itself to be a collective weapon if you'd like. That it also contains the souls of your family would make sense as to masking you as an Abyssal, as they're trying to mask your power if invonvenient. I'll leave it up to you if you want to make your cutlery a weapon or not, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think I'll save the weapon stats for a later evocation, and keep it as mundane weapon for now. Would the vile anathema shroud be an evocation or a passive attunement bonus? I have a charm slot I left open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T09:42:20-08:00","id":1170204,"title":"","content":"I'd say that it would be an evocation. The effect strikes me as too good to be a passive attunement bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T09:43:11-08:00","id":1170205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1168272-ooc-exalted-3e-the-pirates-of-the-gilded-throne?p=1170204#post1170204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that it would be an evocation. The effect strikes me as too good to be a passive attunement bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool. What would be the costs? Indefinite, but how many motes need to be committed to the effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T09:46:17-08:00","id":1170207,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm. I'll say 3m. Ordinarily, I'd go higher, but you are commiting notes to the artifact, so I lessened the cost to offset that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","user":"Dietaku","date":".  Edited bevause i had a change of heart about charm costs 12-24-2017, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T17:43:06-08:00","id":1170326,"title":"","content":"Correct me if I'm wrong. Wyld Shaping costs 2 exp per rolling phase right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T04:43:04-08:00","id":1170404,"title":"","content":"Okay then, anything further I need to do with my sheet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T04:57:54-08:00","id":1170408,"title":"","content":"Mhhm just a suggestion, but what about replacing the two point demense and HS with a single 3dot manse. Not only does it save you a point, you'd have acess to the demense boni at all times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T05:05:25-08:00","id":1170409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1168272-ooc-exalted-3e-the-pirates-of-the-gilded-throne?p=1170408#post1170408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mhhm just a suggestion, but what about replacing the two point demense and HS with a single 3dot manse. Not only does it save you a point, you'd have acess to the demense boni at all times.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The stone I want is not availiable to manses. Since I have the hearthstone and the manse I still get the benefits, I just need to pay an extra dot for the stone I want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T09:10:29-08:00","id":1170449,"title":"","content":"Ok here is the Backstory for Five Lessons Learned.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> To many a visitor Champoor is a wonderous city, it's many illicit thrills accenuated by a subtle sense of danger that only serves to heighten the pleasure one may gain from them. To a native this sense of adventure fades fast, leaving only behind only a feeling of danger and the burning desire to be the abuser, rather than be the abused. The wealthy and powerful of Champoor live a life of decadent wealth, influence and can count on the protection of corrupt gods, bought with sacrifices others make in their name. The majority of the populace however lives a life in squalor. Those who have it good, comparativly, work as bodyguards, assassins, spies or courtesans. Those who have it less good band together as thugs, sell their body for a meal or get sold into slavery outright.<br /> <br /> When Slippery Shadow was born, he belonged to the latter. His mother was a prostitute, he never learned who his father was. Barely getting by herself, she nevertheless choose to share what little she had with him. Despite the other kids in the slum who beat him up regularily for fun, despite the contempt of those of higher station, it was this kindness that perhaps touched him the most. As long as he and his mother had each other, he knew everything would be allright. And he was going to make sure they'd be allright. So he did the only thing he could think of to pull them out of the swamp of squalor they lived in, he stole what they needed from others. It started with food at the markets, but soon after he figured out how to cut the purse of a careless tourist without their notice. They did good. His mother was uneasy with his theft, but ultimatly only said &quot;As long as a deed is done with good intentions in mind, as long as you act upon love, not greed, it's a good deed.&quot; Of course it couldn't last.<br /> <br /> In the end it was not a disease, not a customers rage, greed or perverse desires that struck down his mother. He didn't steal from the wrong people, either. It was politics. All that Shadow knew was that when he got home one day before the onset of calibration, his mother had been killed. Tortured, too. As he stared in shock he missed the hooded shade in the room completly. It's here that he would have died, hadn't the assassin stepped onto a loose floorboard, shocking him out of his own dazed stupor. The knife left a burning streak on his flesh, but didn't bury into his innards. Desperatly he dodged a second blow, then a third. Before a fourth came at him he slammed the door into the assailants face and ran for his life, hiding in a little nieche, crying in silence as his attacker slipped past him, searching. Rage overcame him. He slipped from the shadows and rammed his blade into the assassins back. He pulled it out and stabbed him again, his voice an incoherent howl. Five times he struck and afterwards the murderer of the only person he held dear in life lay before him in a pool of his own blood, his breath wheezing, pain distorting his features, but alive. Then the man laughed, as well as he could anyhow, silently, ragged, but clearly laughter. With sad eyes he offered Slippery Shadow a deal. The name of the man who had paid him to kill his family in exchange for a quick death. Shadow agreed.<br /> <br /> As it turned out he had been hired by some powerful buisness tycoon. Rage burned in Shadows chest and so without a thought for the consequences he went to the merhcant princes mansion, sneaking past guards and servants alike. He found his awnsers deep within the mansion. There the merchant prince sat and drank tea with a remarkable man radiating an allmost palpable sense of power. Quiet, reigning in his rage, fear and sorrow he sat and listened. The man sitting together with the merchant prince turned out to be a veritable demigod. A Dragon Blood, prince of the earth from Kamthahar he had buisness in town some 18 years ago. However he'd had a few ... dozen indiscretions while in town, potentially producing offspring that right now, as he was in the midst of preparation for a prestigious marriage, could produce slightly awkward. Loose ends needed to be tied up and the merchant prince ensured that he had allready taken care of it. They just sat there, drank tea and calmly discussed buisness and exchanged pleasantries while men in their employ murdered, tortured women who couldn't defend themselves and their children. Bitter grief wracked his mind. He was older than that, a grown man. His mother hadn't even become pregnant from this piece of human garbage and yet he had had her killed without blinking an eye. He dared not move. At some point they would be distracted. And he would kill this man. He didn't care about what would happen afterwards. This man would die tonight and if that meant his own death, he would die with a smile.<br /> <br /> His moment eventually came. A man wrapped in dark tunics arrived, bowing before the master of the house and pronouced that the deed was done. The whores and their offspring dead, their lives made an offering to Tenepeshu. However there had been a complication. One of the children had turned out to truly be her fathers daughter, killing three men in a surge of poisionous essence before knocked unconscious by one of their number who died for his heroic act with his own life. They carried her in, barely a grown woman, thin and malnourished. The men rose and the dragon blood unslung his bow, aiming to end the life of his own daughter. Slippery Shadow rose from his hiding place and silently strode over to the men whose attention was focussed solely on the inanimate, beaten figure to their feet. He gripped his knife harder. Just two more paces and he would be in range, plunging his knife into the hated mans back. Then something happened that he did not expect. He smelled something. The girl on the floor smelled like roses. Just like the perfume his mother had used to put on. He grimaced and stopped for just one heartbeat. An innocent was going to die in front of him and all he could think of was murdering another man. He though about what his mother had told him, that good deeds are born of love, not hate or rage. This man in front of him deserved to die, he knew this was true in his heart. He deserved to die for all the suffering he brought to others. But he couldn't kill him, not like he was right now. It didn't matter anyway. An innocent was going to die right in front of him and if he choose his revenge over her life, then he was no better than this man. He came to a descision and as he did he felt new resolve, a reinvigorating power course through his limbs. With a quick motion he threw his knife to the side, against a lavish mirror which loudly shattered. Everyone in the mirror looked towards the mirror for an instant and Shadow ran like he never had before, sliding between two men on the floor and picking up the slightly stirring girl on the ground. The men, merchant, assassin, Dragon Blood all snapped back toward him, their eyes going wide. He didn't pay them any attention and just ran. He ran like he never had before, shouts of rage and fear behind him. Out of the room, dodging the spear of a fightened guard with the woman in his arms, he ran out onto a balcony and then jumped with an ease that suprised himself over to another. Arrows flew through the air, but somehow he anticipated their movements, dodging them with an alacrity he would never had thought possible.<br /> <br /> Alas powerful and quick as he had become in an instant, he was not quick enough to escape the wrath of an experienced choosen of the dragons and the divine protectors of the mansion. Big dogs with blazing eyes and coiling, shifting shades of black water took on the pursuit, matching his speed with their own and harried him from all sides, leaving him distracted and exposed. The Arrow struck into his lower calf, the pain forcing him to his knees. Quickly black veins spread out from the wound as poison took hold and the Dragon Blood came into view. He smiled cruelly and said with a tone perverse satisfaction &quot;Die, Anathema.&quot; He loosened his arrow and while Shadow thought all hope lost something grabbed him from behind and yanked him out of the projectiles path. He was drawn back into the shadows. Literally into them. He could still see the dragon blood and his divine pawns staring on in confusion and impotent rage as if through a dark veil. A dark figure emerged from the shadows, tall, strong with four arm. It made no sound as one of its arms flashed forward and broke the neck of one of the dogs, disappearing effortlessly again back into the shadows before anyone else could see it. While everyone else whirled to meet the attacker that must have just emerged, the dark figure emerged behind the dragon blood and struck his shadow with a blur of his four arms, twisting it into a rope that formed around the dragon bloods neck, ripped him into the air and over the balustrade. It was the last thing Slippery Shadow saw before he passed out.<br /> <br /> He dreamed fitfully that night, then pure sweet nothingness enveloped him. When he woke he was in a forest, miles south of Champoor. His wounds were healed and the strange dark man with four arms stood before him. He regarded Shadow in silence for a while and just as the young man wanted to speak the dark outline of a man raised his own voice, introducing himself as Five Days Darkness, the first Shadow cast by the Unconquered Sun himself and god of calibration. He explained that Slippery Shadow had inherited the Legacy of Shadows Grace, that an ancient compact stood between his soul and exaltation and the dark god. He told him that he had come to see for himself what form this latest incarnation would take and that he was pleased with Shadows guile, grace and compassion, even for one so low as the dragon blooded who had sullied creation with their treachery. He offered Slippery Shadow a choice, to renew the ancient compact once more. Five Days Darkness would teach the young solar the arts and meditations he would need to bring an end to those whose injustice could no longer be tolerated. He would guide Shadow to become the man he would need to be and help him reach his full potential. In return he would perform one task without question for the dark god, as has every incarnation before him. Slippery Shadow didn't know what to think. But he knew this man had saved his own life and that of the girl just now and that he needed someone to help him make sense of everything that had happened. He agreed. Over the course of the five days of calibration Five Days Darkness thus taught the young solar the five secrets of creation he guards, aswell as a hundred other lessons. Spurred on by the powerful essence of the shade of the most potent of gods Slippery Shadow learned to become like a shadow himself. Finally calibration ended and Five Days Darkness took his leave, gifting Slippery Shadow with words of advise and a potent gift. He told him that he would find something that would help his goals if he would set out to find something called the 'Gilded Throne' and bestowed upon the Fivefold Shadow Bindings. Then he left him with the young woman, which reappeared from the darkness Five Days Darkness had hid her in whole and rejuvenated. Embracing a new life, his second breath, Slippery Shadow renamed himself Five Lessons Learned. He would free Champoor from corrupt gods and men choking it. He would make sure that not even the Princes of the Earth could escape their just punishment. And he would make sure that no innocent in his presence would be hurt. But he also knew that he would need allies and patience to reach his goals.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Fivefold Shadow Bindings are a set of what appears to be black leather bracers, in reality however are pure darkness spun from FDDs essence itself and tied together on the inside with starmetal fibers. It's supposed to be a five dot artifact which I have yet to fully design, but in the end it'll be similar to a stronger version of the belt of shadowwalking, granting a stealth bonus for attunment (prob +5 if the 3dot thing gives +3) and having evocations of its own that help operate in the darkness (seeing in the darkness without issue, merging/stepping through/becoming shadow, maybe permanent evocations that upgrade Ebon Shadow style charms in some way).<br /> <br /> The rescued dragonblood is supposed to be a 4 dot retainer, Rose's First Petal is a 18 y/o freshly exalted wood aspect. We might be able to use her as a figurehead for our company, because otherwise people will prob get suspicious about why a group of mortal traders is so vastly successful (as we invaribly will be due to solar greatness).<br /> <br /> FDD is a high ranking god (E7 in 2e), there is a 2e write up for him in the Scavanger Lands book. He came into being the first time Sol shone, the shadow created by his light. He's a creature of darkness due to his nature and can only act at night (and especially during calibration). He does not oppose the incarnae, he is more of a fanboy that can never approach them because he is banished by their light and especially loves the solars (and more specifically night castes), though their anima also makes him uncomfortable. He has invented Ebon Shadow style and practices all the dragon styles (mostly to kick db ass with it because he hates them for supplanting the solars and finds it ironic to use their own techniques against them) and otherwise has very very powerful secret gathering charms (though they only work if the secret has never been touched by the light of day). He can also create wealth, heal people by sending them into darkness to sleep and invest people (exalts/mortals) with power by infusing them with his darkness (has side effects). He is supposed to be Five Lessons Learned's mentor.<br /> <br /> Not posting the char sheet yet as I want to design the Artifact first and ok that with the st. Also not dead set on charms yet, but he's a stealth supernal night caste who practices ebon shadow style, uses alot of stealth charms (prob going to go more for the combat ones since Hope Last Gasp seems to have the more normally sneaky ones, though he may well learn those in time... Fivefold Shadow Burial is just too good not to take!), some Atheletics and larceny, maybe dodge, investigation too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 12-25-2017, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T09:17:47-08:00","id":1170703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wtaylorjr2001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1168272-ooc-exalted-3e-the-pirates-of-the-gilded-throne?p=1170326#post1170326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong. Wyld Shaping costs 2 exp per rolling phase right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that is correct. I'll have to look at my core to double-check, but that sounds right. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> : Your back-story sounds good. Rest assured, I am very familiar with Five Days Darkness, as he's a regular NPC in my circle's games. If you have any further questions, feel free to send them my way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T13:57:25-08:00","id":1170763,"title":"","content":"Would it be alright if I traded my two artifacts for a war strider as I think I need one? If I used wyld shaping I would llikely have an encounter with fae that are more powerful than me and the circle.. What do you think of a war strider with no or low health that needs to be repaired? A war strider and a greater hearthstone I could fix up in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T15:00:14-08:00","id":1170778,"title":"","content":"I will be okay you having a warstrider. However, bear in mind that if you have it, I'll send tougher foes your way sooner. Still, if that's a thing you're okay with, then, you have my blessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T15:39:27-08:00","id":1170787,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I will start modifying my bio.The War Strider is damaged and I need components to repair it. I need money for the raw materials for he repair. It functions but it has penalties do to its state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T15:48:33-08:00","id":1170788,"title":"","content":"We also should think about how obvious we want to be at this point. I mean Warstriders aren't exactly subtle. Aka chances of dieing to suprise wyld hunt assassination are increasing drastically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T15:59:26-08:00","id":1170791,"title":"","content":"The ship is a large first age artifact also so we are already there. I am hoping I can store the warstrider on the ship. If I cannot, Scholar will shadow the ship. I don't know how large the ship is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T16:06:10-08:00","id":1170794,"title":"","content":"Well I guess we can allways use a normal ship to put up a respectable front to sell the spoils stolen by the evil anathema scourge of the seas.<br /> <br /> Though it doesn't look like your character is especially combat focussed charm wise, not sure how much a warstrider will be able to change in that regard. But I haven't read their section in Arms of the Chosen yet, in 2e they were more like extensive artifact armor and could be relativly easily taken apart by a celestial exalt with good combat charms (assuming the pilot wasn't also a combat monkey in which case he'd have an advantage).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T16:16:54-08:00","id":1170798,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with the ship posessing storage space enough for a warstrider, but ultimately, I'll defer to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4017\" data-vbnamecard=\"4017\">angryicecream</a> as its his ship. So you have any ideas what themes or evocation you want your giant battle much to have, @wtaylorjr2001?<br /> <br /> As per your concerns, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a>, you're in the Threshold. True, Prassad is there, but I'd be equally worried about other raiders wishing to get your giant warmech or themselves compared to those who want you dead for theological reasons. Just a thought to consider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T16:21:45-08:00","id":1170799,"title":"","content":"Its an artifact ship we are all on, Laughter's ship. I don't know if it will be ok with Laughter to stow the war strider on his ship. Scholar is definitely not a warrior as you said. I need the war strider to fight behemoths and upper level fae that would respond to wyld shaping technique. I am still reading Arms of the Chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T16:31:57-08:00","id":1170800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1168272-ooc-exalted-3e-the-pirates-of-the-gilded-throne?p=1170798#post1170798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As per your concerns, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a>, you're in the Threshold. True, Prassad is there, but I'd be equally worried about other raiders wishing to get your giant warmech or themselves compared to those who want you dead for theological reasons. Just a thought to consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well unless these raiders frequently harbor multiple exalted of whatever kind they're probably a bit less of a concern than a wyld hunt sporting anywhere from 5-10 well trained experienced dragon blooded versed in immaculate martial arts and equipped with top grade artifacts. But yeah pride goeth before the fall and all that. Maybe mortals are a bit more of a threat in 3e than they used to be, I'm not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T16:33:37-08:00","id":1170801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1168272-ooc-exalted-3e-the-pirates-of-the-gilded-throne?p=1170798#post1170798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fine with the ship posessing storage space enough for a warstrider, but ultimately, I'll defer to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4017\" data-vbnamecard=\"4017\">angryicecream</a> as its his ship. So you have any ideas what themes or evocation you want your giant battle much to have, @wtaylorjr2001?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea. I was hoping to learn about it &quot;in character&quot; and start repairing it. I read that war striders can battle behemoths and the stronger fae that attack Solars who are using Wyld Shaping Technique. I just want to be ready for them, to have a shot at surviving. Scholar will have to learn to pilot it in character, learn the evocations in character and so on. I am hoping it won't be in play for a while as he has to to learn to use it. The die roll I think for encounters is 2 to 11,so there is a good chance of strong opponents with the penalty for each phase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T16:46:57-08:00","id":1170803,"title":"","content":"Yeah we probably should build a bit of a powerbase and get up to maybe Essence two before we start playing around with Wyld Shaping Technique. With bad luck we could easily face an army of fae which then gets joined by a behemoth which then gets joined by....<br /> <br /> Doing it right out of the gate seems pretty risky, even with a war strider in tow.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T16:54:42-08:00","id":1170804,"title":"","content":"I have no intention of using wyld shaping technique out of the bat. Scholar's goals are to find his sister, change his sister back to normal if necessary, and fix his war strider. I need exp for wyld shaping, a lot of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T17:01:34-08:00","id":1170805,"title":"","content":"Ok I've finished my charsheet. First Binding: Cloak of Shadows and Slip from View are evocations of the Fivefold Shadow Bindings, the former being unlocked upon attunement for free, which is why his charmcount totals 16 instead of 15. Bps were spent on Abilities and Merits.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hJ-HBFnT7J-uVlgJCeZoV_6q5NnCNxgN/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hJ-...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Stats for his Artifact:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Fivefold Shadow Bindings (Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 )</b></span><br /> <br /> Forged from the Essence of Five Days Darkness bound by Starmetal wires, the Fivefold Shadowbindings look like a pair of leather bracers to be tied tightly around the arms. Each of the bracers seems to consist of five black leather straps, if touched however they are unnaturally cold and give little tactile feedback, giving the feeling of touching nothing at all. On the inside small Starmetal wires can be seen binding the shadows together. It costs five motes to attune the Fivefold Shadow Bindings. Both Solars and (to Five Days Darkness' chagrin) Sidereals are resonant to them. An attuned user adds five dice to all stealth rolls as the Bindings call to shadows to hide their bearer.<br /> <br /> Evocations:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>First Binding: Cloak of Shadows</b></span><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mute, Resonant<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Suffused with the Essence of the highest of shadows, the bearer of the Fivefold Shadow Bindings becomes one with Darkness. Tenebrous darkness<br /> flows out of the bracers to cover the whole body of its wearer, turning her indistinguishable and perfectly concealing her identity.<br /> This is in effect similar to the inherent power of the Night Caste Anima at bonfire level, however it does not require the Anima to flare<br /> (and hence does not inhibit stealth). This is treated as a perfect effect, it cannot be pierced by magic lesser than Eyes Of The Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> Resonant: The wearer becomes fully at home in the darkness that envelops him, ignoring penalties associated with darkness (such as poor visibility).<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: A character attuning to the Fivefold Shadow Bindings during Calibration unlocks this Evocation for free. This evocation can only be unlocked during Calibration.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Slip from View</b></span><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: First Binding: Cloak of Shadows<br /> <br /> Every light casts a shadow. Even on a bright day on a plain field, the wearer of the Fivefold Shadow Bindings can hide. Supplementing an attempt to establish stealth with this charm allows the wearer to do so even if there are no means of concealment present. Instead he hides within his own shadow, which in return hides within the shadows of every other person present.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Flickering Essence Internalization</b></span><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Ebon Shadow Form<br /> <br /> The Essence of Five Days Darkness flows through the bindings, enhancing the style that he crafted himself. A character learning this charm unlocks the Mastery effects of the Ebon Shadow style Charms, up to and including the Form charm.<br /> <br /> Resonant: Going beyond normal mastery of this Style, the Bindings further enhance the prowess of a Solar or Sidereal, granting the following benefits.<br /> <br /> Nothing But Shadows: The penalty imposed becomes higher of Stealth or 3.<br /> <br /> Seven Points Of Weakness Strike: If this charm aids an unexpected attack, it also adds the wearers Essence to the amount of ignored armor.<br /> <br /> Ebon Shadow Form: Activating Ebon Shadow form now also activates First Binding: Cloak of Shadows at no additional cost. This effect cannot be voluntarily turned off.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: This evocation is learned at no cost the first time the wearer kills a non trivial opponent while wearing the Cloak of Shadows in accordance with a major intimacy.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Second Binding: Become the Shadow</b></span><br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisites: First Binding: Cloak of Shadows<br /> <br /> The character becomes a shadow. She turns immaterial and may pass through small cracks, though barriers without any openings still bar his passage. In darkness she becomes near invisible, but in well lit rooms characters will notice a stray shadow upon passing a difficulty 3 (Perception + Awareness) roll, unless mundane stealth is employed (and resolved normally). While using this charm the wearer has no scent and makes no sound. If the character uses charms that normally would allow her to affect immaterial beings while being immaterial, he can use this charm to affect material beings instead. After a scene has passed he must stay material for at least 10 minutes.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Shadow Hand</b></span><br /> Cost: 1m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Second Binding: Become the Shadow<br /> <br /> Suffusing her shadow with Essence the wearer grasps the material while immaterial or vice versa.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: If the wearer learns Spirit-Cutting Attack this functionally identical evocation is unlocked for free as soon as the prerequisites are learned.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Breathstealing Exercise</b></span><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Shadow Hand<br /> <br /> The wearer of the Fivefold Shadow Bindings learns to strangle another with her own essence infused tenebrous form. This evocation supplements a special grapple gambit undertaken while immaterial through the use of Become The Shadow. Twisting her own form into a blanket the wearer twist himself around the opponents head, strangling her victim slowly. This special grappling gambit differs in the following ways from a normal grapple:<ul><li>The wearer has to use Breathstealing Exercise every turn in order to maintain the grapple, failing to do so automatically ends the grapple with the targets release.</li> <li>Only the Savage move can be taken. Instead of applying damage as normal this move inflicts one point of bashing damage (Hardness does not apply) directly to the opponents health track. Once the opponents health track is filled with bashing damage each additional turn transforms one point of bashing damage into lethal damage. Opponents who do not need to breathe are immune to this damage.</li> <li>The roll to control the grapple is (Dexterity + Brawl or Martial Arts) on the side of the attacker opposed by the enemies (Dexterity + Dodge) or (Strength + Brawl or Martial Arts) in case of an opponent capable of affecting immaterial beings.</li> <li>The victim of the grapple is blinded, muted and deafened. As the wearer wraps himself around his victim, these selfsame penalties apply to her.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Vanishing Shadow Meditation</b></span><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Resonant<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Shadow-Body Dissolution, Flickering Essence Internalization<br /> <br /> Furthering her understanding of the Ebon Shadow Style, the wearer applies the Mastery effect to Elusive Flicker Evasion, even if she normally would not and removes the Terrestrial tag from Elusive Flicker Evasion and Shadow-Body Dissolution should the wearer be affected by it.<br /> <br /> Resonant: Going beyond normal mastery of this Style, the Bindings further enhance the prowess of a Solar or Sidereal, granting the following benefits.<br /> <br /> Elusive Flicker Evasion: This charm loses the Decisive-only tag and gains the Uniform tag instead, enabling its use against withering attacks.<br /> <br /> Shadow-Body Dissolution: If no damage is taken from the attack and Stealth successfully established, the Martial Artists also gains (Essence) initiative.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: This evocation is learned at no cost the first time a character avoids being hit completely or reduces damage of a decisive attack made against him to zero using the prerequisite charms in a fight where he upholds a major intimacy.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Fear The Dark</b></span><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only, Resonant<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Seven Points Weakness Strike, First Binding: Cloak of Shadows<br /> <br /> Exploiting the weakness of his opponents from the dark, the wearer of the Fivefold Shadow Bindings surrounds his hands with darkened essence, striking fear into his target. The wearer uses a gambit costing (Resolve+1) initiative making an unexpected (Manipulation + Stealth) based decisive attack against a difficulty of the targets Resolve or Defense, whichever is higher (Resolve does not take penalties against unexpected attacks and the appearance of the attacker does not matter). If successful this instills an intimacy of fear towards darkness or strengthens such an intimacy if it already exists. While Cloak of Shadows is active, the wearer counts as darkness for the purposes of this intimacy.<br /> <br /> Resonant: This gambit can be used without establishing stealth first as long as Cloak of Shadows is active.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Third Binding: Secret Stealing Claw</b></span><br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Second Binding: Become the Shadow<br /> <br /> Five Days Darkness has knowledge of all secrets residing in the dark, even those hiding within the darkness of the soul. The wearer executes a quick jab at the targets shadow, ripping dark thoughts out of it as a ball of shadowy essence which she then swallows. This charm represents a Gambit rolled against a difficulty of the targets Guile. If successful, the character learns the characters darkest secret, the one thing he most desperately wants to stay concealed.<br /> <br /> Resonant: This Gambit can be used as part of an Ambush, increasing its difficulty by two. If successful, no combat is initiated, the target does not perceive any overt hostile attempt behind the attack.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Infinite Shadow Panoply</b></span><br /> Cost: 5m,; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisites: Umbra Noose Execution<br /> <br /> Twisting his own shadow into a weapon, the wearer creates the shadowy equivalent of one of the Ebon Shadow styles form weapons (or a pair thereof in case of weapons which can be wielded as pairs). These weapons have the tags and properties of their respective artifact weapons.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Dark Executioner Enlightenment</b></span><br /> Cost: -,; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Resonant<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Umbra Noose Execution, Vanishing Shadow Meditation<br /> <br /> Fully in tune with the Essence of Five Days Darkness, the exalt ignores the Terrestrial Keyword of Throat-Slitting Shadow Artemi and gains the Mastery keyword for Umbra Noose Execution.<br /> <br /> Resonant: When Resonant with the Fivefold Shadow Bindings the techniques of Ebon Shadow Style are further enhanced:<br /> <br /> Throat-Slitting Shadow Artemi: By increasing the cost to 3m, 1wp the character can change the effect of Throat slitting Artemi. Instead of converting the damage dice into successes, the charm doubles the damage of a decisive attack after rolling. This cannot enhance the damage rolled by more than (Essence) unless the attack was unexpected and does not stack with charms like Thunderbolt Attack Prana that have a similar effect.<br /> <br /> Umbra Noose Execution: The motes are stolen by the charm instantly and lost to the victim without any positive effect.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: This evocation is learned at no cost the first time the wearer uses Throat-Slitting Artemi or Umbra Noose Execution to kill a non trivial opponent in adherence to a defining Intimacy.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Paralyzing Touch Attack</b></span><br /> Cost: 5m,; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Resonant<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Umbra Noose Execution<br /> <br /> The wearer of the Fivefold Shadow Bindings hones in on his targets weakness, paralyzing it with a strike to one of five vital nerve clusters. This is a gamble using (Dexterity + Martial Arts) and costing (opponents Stamina x2) Initiative. The wearer makes a decisive attack which inflicts no damage. Instead the target takes a penalty to all Dexterity derived dicepools (including dicepools used to calculate Defense) equal to the Threshold successes on the roll, to a maximum of the attackers (Essence).<br /> <br /> Resonant: Reduce the Initiative cost of this maneuver to (Stamina + 1).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Blow Concealing Gesture</b></span><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform, Resonant<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Umbra Noose Execution, Third Binding: Secret Stealing Claw, Slip From View<br /> <br /> The wearers hands flash through the motions of danger unnoticed, concealing his killing intent from the opponent. This evocation supplements an attack that is not unexpected. Roll (Dexterity + Stealth) opposed by the targets (Perception + Awareness). If successful, the attack becomes unexpected.<br /> <br /> Resonant: Add half the threshold successes (rounded up) to your initiative.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Fourth Binding: Day As Night Stance</b></span><br /> Cost: 10m,; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisites: Third Binding: Secret Stealing Claw<br /> <br /> The wearer of the Fivefold Shadow Bindings flashes through a quick series of five stances that symbolize the importance of calibration. Once he finishes the Bindings expand, creating a patch of pure darkness out to medium range. Mundane senses fail to pierce this concealment and lightsources fail to produce any light. Supernatural sight pierces this darkness but takes a penalty to all rolls involving sight equal to the bearers essence.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Shadow Banishment</b></span><br /> Cost: 8m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Umbra Noose Execution, Fear The Dark, Breathstealing Exercise<br /> <br /> Sometimes it's not enough to kill an enemy or to simply frighten him. The worst of the worst deserve a special torment. A series of lightning quick jabs infects the target with shadow essence and a final push condemn him to a most impotent exile. The wearer executes a gambit making a (Dexterity + Martial Arts) based decisive attack costing the targets (Essence +1) initiative. If successful the target is pushed into his own shadow, fusing with it. The target is thereafter forever banished from the material world. Treat him as if he were under the effects of \u201cSecond Binding: Become the Shadow\u201d, but the change is permanent. The only way for the target to become material again is for it to possess a charm that allows it to materialize (or temporarily immaterialize), a successful Celestial tier sorcerous working done on his behalf or for the wearer of the Fivefold Shadow Bindings to use this charm again on his shadow, reversing the effects.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Shadow Wanderer</b></span><br /> Cost: 10m; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Shadow-Stepping Motion<br /> <br /> Becoming a friend to shadows, the wearer can move along them with greater ease. This evocation allows the wearer of the Fivefold Shadow Bindings to travel two range bands by stepping into one shadow and emerging from another. Just like it's prerequisite this adds double 9s and removes the penalty for crossing open terrain from any stealth rolls. In combat use of this charm counts as the characters movement and combat action.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Fifth Binding: Shadow-Plumbing Gaze</b></span><br /> Cost: 20m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Fourth Binding: Day As Night Stance<br /> <br /> The wearer stands still for five minutes, meditating on the essence of Five Days Darkness, before replicating one of his greatest feats. The wearer slips past the shadows of the world and watches the skeins of discarded fates behind the curtain of creation, searching through them for answers This Evocation creates a special (Perception + Investigation) action with a difficulty set by the storyteller appropriate to the secret the character tries to uncover. If successful the wearer discovers the information he seeks as a series of vision, conversation snippets and instinctive insights. However this power has two downsides. It can only be used once per story, and no effect can reset it early except for the onset of calibration. Secondly if the information sought has \u201cseen the light of day\u201d (enough people know about it, it has been discussed in broad daylight or some important aspect of it such as a murder weapon has been touched by sunlight) the evocation automatically fails.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> For conviniences sake we can say he also found his way to the group at that battle in Alabaster (though he probably would have approached you after the battle, given his strong Stealth focus its kind of unlike that anyone except perhaps Diane would have spotted his presence [though there may have been some fairies who very conviniently had been taken out by someone just as you had turned your back]), alternativly we could stage a first meeting in some fashion in flotsam where he is trying to figure out what the gilded throne is and where to find it. He's unlikely to reveal himself as a solar unless someone else does to first though.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 12-26-2017, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T18:07:09-08:00","id":1170818,"title":"","content":"@Flinty: In my experience, fighting mortals is scarier than fighting them in 2e, but not by much. You won't crap out huge damage to one shot them much anymore; dicepools don't balloon as fast as they did in 2e, but a Solar even with modest fighting charm proficiency and an artifact weapon can make short work of most mortal threats. Its just that they can and will take a few licks in so doing. However, I'm not just talking of mortals, or even Dragonbloods, but... Others. That's all I'll say.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> : Very well, then. I'll make a suitably cool back-story and loadout for your war mech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T18:24:03-08:00","id":1170821,"title":"","content":"On: Rose's First Petal (or Rose for short, now that I think about it I wonder how Hope's Last Gasp will react to that): 18-19 y/o, relativly freshly exalted wood aspect. Daughter of a Prostitue, so probably was forced to take that job up herself. Lost everything when she was nearly assassinated. Stays with Lessons out of a mixture of gratitude and burning desire for revenge (the two of them plan to liberate Champoor from its corrupt gods... and have some sweet vengence on the side). Any further personality quirks, dark secrets or whatever I'd leave up to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1586_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1586\" data-vbnamecard=\"1586\">Dietaku</a><br /> Probably favours social attributes and abilities. In combat would likely use thrown weapons (or archery, whichever you prefer, though thrown weapons are usually easier concealed and smuggled into a social setting) and poison, which as a wood aspect she could probably produce herself via charms. (.... OH god my char is batman and she is poison ivy....)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T18:31:58-08:00","id":1170824,"title":"","content":"If it will make it easier for you I got the mech on page 147 of arms of the chosen, .Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation. If it's ok with you I would like it to be damaged. I have first age crafting and would like to try my hand at repairing it. I would like to try and package it in a huge crate and put it in Laughter's cargo hold if its OK with AngryIcecream. I don't want to step on the stealth peoples shoes. Scholar would try to &quot;hide&quot; it in a huge box so others won't know what it is. I am still working on the adjusted bio. I am going to say it takes most of my fortune to acquire and transport the mech to the ship.This is why Scholar has a Resource of one.<br /> <br /> One question: The hearthstone that it takes to power the mech, can it be any greater hearthstone? If so I would use a gem of inner power to power the mecha. If its OK I would have the free evocation it gives be used for one of the mecha's evocations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T18:52:06-08:00","id":1170830,"title":"","content":"Doesn't scholar focus on meele? The Cathedral seems mostly intended for long range combat using archery weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T18:55:36-08:00","id":1170831,"title":"","content":"Thanks for catching that. It's late and I need sleep. All-Conquering Colossus on page 144. Excuse the heck out of me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T07:36:05-08:00","id":1170940,"title":"","content":"Darn, and here I was hoping I could flex my muscles a bit creatively. Oh well, if one of the prefab warstriders is what you want, go ahead. As per the gem of hidden power, I suppose that's fine, but know that once more, each power-up you ask for is me conceding to myself that ,&quot; Yeah, they can take tough things right off.&quot; <br /> <br /> If that's fine with you, then go ahead. As per the damage and crate business, that's all good. I have no problem with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T07:48:25-08:00","id":1170942,"title":"","content":"Please feel free to create the warstrider. Whatever is more fun for all of us. I just wanted it to be easy but creating it is better, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I just need your creation to alter my bio to fit it in. I just envision it to be broken really bad requiring me to fix it.<br /> <br /> Postscript: Everything I am asking for is not of use to me so much at the beginning. The warstrider has to be fixed, though it can be used with penalties. The hearthstone can be used if the evocations are for essense 1 Exalts. So bear that in mind before I get overwhelmed with strife. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","user":"wtaylorjr2001","date":". 12-27-2017, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T08:21:45-08:00","id":1170952,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that the gem of inner power is a linked hearthstone and provides no effect unless it is socketed together with another hearthstone. Also it explicitly has to be socketed into an orichalcum weapon, think warstriders would count more as armor... but maybe both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T08:35:22-08:00","id":1170957,"title":"","content":"Oh, no worries. I'm not in the habit of TPKing my curcle's. I'm just trying to be transparent for you. Don't worry, either, I got that you warstrider is broken. I'm not going to toss Draggokaiser, Redcap Ba Rai's Blade, at you, but you may encounter things I'd hold off on sooner, is all. <br /> <br /> As per your war strider, I'll use the stats of All-Conquering Colossus, but I'll write up some new evocation for it this evening. I have some ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T08:36:35-08:00","id":1170958,"title":"","content":"I thought it was linked to a manse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T08:45:51-08:00","id":1170960,"title":"","content":"Ah right my mistake. Mixed up Linked and Dependant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T10:20:14-08:00","id":1170979,"title":"","content":"I would like to register discomfort with the warstrider idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T10:22:55-08:00","id":1170980,"title":"","content":"Why are you uncomfortable with the warstrider Aranfan?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I created a discord server for everyone, it's here: <a href=\"https://discord.gg/csNpvR\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/csNpvR</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T10:31:20-08:00","id":1170983,"title":"","content":"It jacks the stakes up immensely. And right away when we're still getting our feet under us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T10:41:50-08:00","id":1170989,"title":"","content":"My War Strider will be in the ship until it is fixed. I will use it only against things like Behemoths and Fae that come from Wyld Shaping. Besides, I trust Diataku to make an interesting and fun game. First I must get the gold xp to fix it, I think gold is for major tasks. If people find out about it I will have some exp under my belt. We all will. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","user":"wtaylorjr2001","date":". 12-27-2017, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T10:56:00-08:00","id":1170997,"title":"","content":"I think this might not actually be the game for me, but I'm desperate enough to play exalted that I'll give it a try anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T12:09:49-08:00","id":1171021,"title":"","content":"Well a compromise (and fun idea) might be to find the Warstrider over the course of the story. You won't need it immediatly anyway and the storyseeds given specifically mention a mysterious treasure island that could host all kinds of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T12:14:29-08:00","id":1171023,"title":"","content":"I would be much more comfortable with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/ava