lved around the sword, she has mastered the mundane parts of the Single Point Shining Into the Void and Steel Devil Styles.<br /> <br /> To celebrate Shining Topaz's 18<sup>th</sup> birthday, her father held a grand swordfighting tournament that drew fighters from across the land. Shining Topaz entered herself, but the two dragonblooded warriors from Prasad, a father and a son, were the favorites to win the tournament. It was a great upset when, in the semifinals, Shining Topaz managed to defeat the younger Terrestrial Exalt. Yet while the son was newly exalted only a year ago, the Father had been exalted for a century and would not go down so easily.<br /> <br /> At first the fight seemed to go Topaz's way, but then the Exalt smiled and complimented her skill and started spending Essence. On the back foot, it was apparent that the Princess was losing. Then when the Exalt went in for the final blow the impossible happened, Shining Topaz flared with golden light and turned aside the Terrestrial Exalt's blade. Empowered by the Sun, Shining Topaz defeated the Terrestrial and declared that she would become the Invincible Sword Princess.<br /> <br /> However, she had become Solar Anathema right in front of everybody, and the confrontation with her father soon fallowed. Fortunately for her, her earnest enthusiasm for swords, disgust for bureaucracy, and commitment to the proper line of succession convinced her father that she was still herself and not a demon in the skin of his daughter.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately this sealed the fate of the kingdom. Although a fighter without peer, shining Topaz was but one woman, and could not stop Prasad from destroying her home. Fleeing to the Dreaming Sea, with a former naval officer of Terek Laughter upon the Breeze, she was forced to take up piracy to survive and avoid the Wyld Hunts that still dog her heels.<br /> <br /> Should the chance arise, she would love to punish Prasad and restore her elder brother to his rightful throne. 